<p>
      Indeed, <m>L</m> contains zero, and is easily seen to be closed under addition and scalar multiplication.
      </p>
    </example>

    <example>
      <title>A plane through the origin</title>
      <p>A plane <m>P</m> through the origin is a subspace.
      </p>
<image width="60%">
<shortdescription>
